<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} jsonld={jsonld} navVariant="inner">
<section class="hero">
<div class="wrap">
<span class="eyebrow">Seasonal</span>
<h1>Monsoon Watch: July–September, from inside the clusters</h1>
<p class="lead">The cluster doesn't stop for monsoon—it just gets riskier. Monsoon Watch is our free seasonal advisory for buyers with orders in production between July and September.</p>
<div class="hero-ctas"><a class="btn btn-solid" href="/#book">Book an inspection</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/why-independent/">Why independent</a></div>
</div>
</section>
<section><div class="wrap"><div class="grid"><a class="card rv" href="/clusters/jodhpur/"><h3>Moisture physics</h3><p>Humidity stalls drying and re-wets seasoned stock; we tighten moisture limits and extend kiln checks.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/defects/"><h3>Finish behaviour</h3><p>Lacquer blushes and cure times stretch—early finished pieces need longer holds before packing.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/production-monitoring-india/"><h3>Lead-time drift</h3><p>Power, transport and subcontractor delays stack quietly. Vessel dates need buffer, not optimism.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/container-loading-supervision/"><h3>Loading protocol</h3><p>Weather holds enforced at stuffing; rain-exposed cartons pulled. Non-negotiable under CLS L-10.</p></a></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap prose-wrap"><p class="prose rv">Subscribers receive a short advisory at monsoon onset, mid-season and close-out, plus alerts when conditions warrant. It's free—the goal is fewer August surprises for everyone. If you're shipping in this window, our standing recommendation is DUPRO plus PSI plus CLS as a set, not any one alone.</p></div></section>
<section class="final">
<div class="wrap">

<h2>Your next India order. Protected.</h2>
<p>Confirmed within 2 hours. Report within 24 hours of inspection. Paid by buyers only — never by factories.</p>
<a class="btn btn-solid" href="/#book">Book an inspection</a>
</div>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
